Relevant columns and their potential usage
• match.match_id: primary key to identify each match; will be the main link to other fact tables.  
• match.season_id: filter to keep only records that belong to season 5 (condition: match."season_id" = 5).  
• player.player_id: unique id of every player; necessary for joining to get player names.  
• player.player_name: the name we finally want to show.  
• batsman_scored.match_id / over_id / ball_id / runs_scored / innings_no: holds the number of runs credited to the striker on every ball.  
• ball_by_ball.match_id / over_id / ball_id / striker: lets us know which player actually scored the runs in that batsman_scored row.  
• player_match.match_id / player_id: tells us which players took part in a given match; used to count how many matches a player played (denominator for the batting average).  

Main conditions to be used
1. match."season_id" = 5      – restrict to season 5.  
2. batsman_scored."match_id" IN (all season 5 matches) – keep only the scoring events from those matches.  
3. JOIN on match_id + over_id + ball_id between batsman_scored and ball_by_ball to map every run to its scorer (ball_by_ball."striker").  
4. JOIN the scorer id to player.player_id to show the player name.  
5. For batting‑average per player:  
   total_runs = SUM(runs_scored)  
   matches_played = COUNT(DISTINCT player_match."match_id")  
   batting_average = total_runs * 1.0 / matches_played  
6. ORDER BY batting_average DESC and LIMIT 5 to obtain the “top 5” list.

Below are 10 exploratory SQL queries—each different, gradually increasing in complexity—so you can inspect intermediate data and finally retrieve the requested result.  
All queries use SELECT only, apply DISTINCT where reasonable, and return no more than 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List all distinct seasons available in the match table (sanity check).
SELECT DISTINCT "season_id"
FROM "match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show 20 sample matches from season 5.
SELECT "match_id",
       "team_1",
       "team_2",
       "match_date",
       "venue"
FROM "match"
WHERE "season_id" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Pick one season‑5 match and look at the first 20 scoring events in batsman_scored.
SELECT bs."match_id",
       bs."over_id",
       bs."ball_id",
       bs."runs_scored",
       bs."innings_no"
FROM   "batsman_scored" AS bs
WHERE  bs."match_id" IN (SELECT "match_id" FROM "match" WHERE "season_id" = 5)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join batsman_scored to ball_by_ball for a single match
--                 to view which batsman (striker) scored each recorded run.
SELECT bb."match_id",
       bb."over_id",
       bb."ball_id",
       bb."striker"      AS "player_id",
       bs."runs_scored"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
       ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
       AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
       AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
WHERE  bb."match_id" = (
           SELECT "match_id"
           FROM "match"
           WHERE "season_id" = 5
           LIMIT 1
       )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Aggregate runs per player (striker) for that same single match.
SELECT bb."striker"          AS "player_id",
       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "runs_in_match"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
       ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
       AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
       AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
WHERE  bb."match_id" = (
           SELECT "match_id"
           FROM "match"
           WHERE "season_id" = 5
           LIMIT 1
       )
GROUP BY bb."striker"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Total runs scored by every batsman across ALL season‑5 matches.
SELECT bb."striker"          AS "player_id",
       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs_season5"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
       ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
       AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
       AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
WHERE  bb."match_id" IN (
           SELECT "match_id"
           FROM "match"
           WHERE "season_id" = 5
       )
GROUP BY bb."striker"
ORDER BY "total_runs_season5" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: How many season‑5 matches each player *appeared* in (using player_match).
SELECT pm."player_id",
       COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played_s5"
FROM   "player_match" AS pm
WHERE  pm."match_id" IN (
           SELECT "match_id"
           FROM "match"
           WHERE "season_id" = 5
       )
GROUP BY pm."player_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Combine the last two sub‑totals (runs and matches) into one view.
SELECT  r."player_id",
        r."total_runs_season5",
        m."matches_played_s5"
FROM  (
        SELECT bb."striker" AS "player_id",
               SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs_season5"
        FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
        JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
               ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
               AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
               AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
        WHERE  bb."match_id" IN (
                   SELECT "match_id"
                   FROM "match"
                   WHERE "season_id" = 5
               )
        GROUP BY bb."striker"
     ) AS r
JOIN (
        SELECT pm."player_id",
               COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played_s5"
        FROM   "player_match" AS pm
        WHERE  pm."match_id" IN (
                   SELECT "match_id"
                   FROM "match"
                   WHERE "season_id" = 5
               )
        GROUP BY pm."player_id"
     ) AS m
     ON r."player_id" = m."player_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Compute batting average (runs per match) and show top 20 players.
SELECT  sub."player_id",
        sub."total_runs_season5",
        sub."matches_played_s5",
        sub."total_runs_season5" * 1.0 / sub."matches_played_s5" AS "batting_average"
FROM (
        /* same subquery as #8 */
        SELECT  r."player_id",
                r."total_runs_season5",
                m."matches_played_s5"
        FROM  (
                SELECT bb."striker" AS "player_id",
                       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs_season5"
                FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
                JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
                       ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
                       AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
                       AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
                WHERE  bb."match_id" IN (
                           SELECT "match_id"
                           FROM "match"
                           WHERE "season_id" = 5
                       )
                GROUP BY bb."striker"
             ) AS r
        JOIN (
                SELECT pm."player_id",
                       COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played_s5"
                FROM   "player_match" AS pm
                WHERE  pm."match_id" IN (
                           SELECT "match_id"
                           FROM "match"
                           WHERE "season_id" = 5
                       )
                GROUP BY pm."player_id"
             ) AS m
             ON r."player_id" = m."player_id"
     ) AS sub
ORDER BY "batting_average" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL answer – names of top‑5 players with highest average
--                  runs per match in season 5 (batting average = runs / matches).
SELECT  p."player_name",
        ROUND(sub."total_runs_season5" * 1.0 / sub."matches_played_s5", 2) AS "batting_average"
FROM (
        SELECT  r."player_id",
                r."total_runs_season5",
                m."matches_played_s5"
        FROM  (
                SELECT bb."striker" AS "player_id",
                       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs_season5"
                FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS bb
                JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS bs
                       ON  bb."match_id" = bs."match_id"
                       AND bb."over_id"  = bs."over_id"
                       AND bb."ball_id"  = bs."ball_id"
                WHERE  bb."match_id" IN (
                           SELECT "match_id"
                           FROM "match"
                           WHERE "season_id" = 5
                       )
                GROUP BY bb."striker"
             ) AS r
        JOIN (
                SELECT pm."player_id",
                       COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played_s5"
                FROM   "player_match" AS pm
                WHERE  pm."match_id" IN (
                           SELECT "match_id"
                           FROM "match"
                           WHERE "season_id" = 5
                       )
                GROUP BY pm."player_id"
             ) AS m
             ON r."player_id" = m."player_id"
     ) AS sub
JOIN "player" AS p
     ON p."player_id" = sub."player_id"
ORDER BY (sub."total_runs_season5" * 1.0 / sub."matches_played_s5") DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

The last query will return exactly the required information: the names of the five best performers in season 5 together with their batting averages (runs per match).
